{"tool_name":"censor","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"censor","home":"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/Tools/so/censor/","summary":"Protein and nucleotide sequence repeat identification and masking. Screens query sequences against a reference collection of repeats and \"censors\" (masks) homologous portions with masking symbols, as well as generating a report classifying all found repeats.","addition_date":"2015-01-29T15:47:46Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:03:54.087012Z","tool_type":["Web application","Web service"],"version":["Retired"],"collections":["EBI Tools"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:censor","credit":[{"name":"EMBL-EBI","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"GIRI","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"Oleksiy Kohany","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"Job Dispatcher","typeEntity":"Project","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/Tools/jdispatcher/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/Tools/so/censor/"},{"type":["Terms of use"],"url":"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/about/terms-of-use"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["biomadeira","nandana"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2044"}}],"operation":[{"term":"Repeat sequence detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0379"},{"term":"Sequence masking","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0368"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid features","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1276"}}]}],"maturity":"Legacy","name":"CENSOR (EBI)","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"jdispatcher","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkac240","metadata":{"abstract":"The EMBL-EBI search and sequence analysis tools frameworks provide integrated access to EMBL-EBI's data resources and core bioinformatics analytical tools. EBI Search (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ebisearch) provides a full-text search engine across nearly 5 billion entries, while the Job Dispatcher tools framework (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/services) enables the scientific community to perform a diverse range of sequence analysis using popular bioinformatics applications. Both allow users to interact through user-friendly web applications, as well as via RESTful and SOAP-based APIs. Here, we describe recent improvements to these services and updates made to accommodate the increasing data requirements during the COVID-19 pandemic.","authors":[{"name":"Basutkar P."},{"name":"Edbali O."},{"name":"Kolesnikov A."},{"name":"Lee J."},{"name":"Lopez R."},{"name":"Madeira F."},{"name":"Madhusoodanan N."},{"name":"Pearce M."},{"name":"Tivey A.R.N."}],"citationCount":1248,"date":"2022-07-05T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"Search and sequence analysis tools services from EMBL-EBI in 2022"},"pmcid":"PMC9252731","pmid":"35412617","type":["Other"]},{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkv1352","metadata":{"abstract":"New technologies are revolutionising biological research and its applications by making it easier and cheaper to generate ever-greater volumes and types of data. In response, the services and infrastructure of the European Bioinformatics Institute (EMBL-EBI, www.ebi.ac.UK) are continually expanding: total disk capacity increases significantly every year to keep pace with demand (75 petabytes as of December 2015), and interoperability between resources remains a strategic priority. Since 2014 we have launched two new resources: the European Variation Archive for genetic variation data and EMPIAR for two-dimensional electron microscopy data, as well as a Resource Description Framework platform. We also launched the Embassy Cloud service, which allows users to run large analyses in a virtual environment next to EMBL-EBI's vast public data resources.","authors":[{"name":"Apweiler R."},{"name":"Bergman M.T."},{"name":"Birney E."},{"name":"Cochrane G."},{"name":"Cook C.E."},{"name":"Finn R.D."}],"citation